How do the chlorine atoms released from CFCs interact with ozone molecules in the stratosphere, leading to ozone depletion?
Chlorine atoms (Cl) react with ozone molecules (O3) to remove one oxygen atom, leaving O and chlorine monoxide (ClO). ClO then reacts with ozone to release two O molecules and a Cl atom, which remains in the system as a radical, continuing the catalytic cycle and leading to ozone depletion.
