What is the history of the Academy Awards and when did they introduce categories for foreign films?
The Academy Awards, presented by the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences (AMPAS), have a history dating back to 1929. Initially, there was no separate category for foreign language films. The first Academy Awards ceremony took place on May 16, 1929, to honor films released in 1927/28. Between 1947 and 1955, the Academy presented Special/Honorary Awards to the best foreign language films.
